windres: zero coff_info on resources read from a .res file.

bin_to_res() leaves the resource's coff_info for the caller to fill, and the
.res reader read_resource_entry() never does, while rescoff.c writes
coff_info.codepage and coff_info.reserved into every COFF resource data
entry. So `windres` turning a .res into a COFF object emits 8 bytes of
uninitialized heap per resource: the output is not deterministic. Not
platform-specific; affects every host.

--- a/binutils/resres.c	2026-09-15 18:42:34.823772861 -0300
+++ b/binutils/resres.c	2026-09-15 18:42:34.847771914 -0300
@@ -216,6 +216,9 @@
   /* Convert binary data to resource */
   r = bin_to_res (wrbfd, type, buff, reshdr.data_size);
   r->res_info = resinfo;
+  /* bin_to_res leaves coff_info to the caller; rescoff.c writes it into
+     every COFF resource data entry.  */
+  memset (&r->coff_info, 0, sizeof (r->coff_info));
   /* Add resource to resource directory */
   res_add_resource (r, &type, &name, resinfo.language, 0);
 
